---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="The Issue">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">The Issue</span>
      <h1>Energy is the climate problem we use every day.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Every lecture hall, lab, and dorm room runs on electricity. Where that power comes from shapes our campus's
        impact on the planet.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 0">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="stat">
        <strong class="placeholder">[X%]</strong>
        <p>
          <span class="placeholder">[PLACEHOLDER: add a sourced stat, e.g. share of Georgia's electricity from fossil fuels]</span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section band">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <h2>Why it matters to students</h2>
        <p>
          Today's students will live with the results of today's energy choices. Clean energy cuts emissions, improves
          air quality, and builds the skills and industries our generation will work in.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2>What clean energy looks like</h2>
        <ul class="checklist">
          <li><strong>Solar power</strong> on rooftops and parking areas</li>
          <li><strong>Energy efficiency</strong> in buildings and labs</li>
          <li><strong>Smarter grids</strong> that use power when it's cleanest</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>So what can we do?</h2>
      <p class="lead">Learn the facts, then join students already working on solutions.</p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/get-involved">See how to get involved</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
